<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nineteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nineteenth Amendment to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">United States Constitution</a>, ratified in August 1920, prohibits the federal government and the states from denying citizens the right to vote on account of sex. It was the culmination of the women's suffrage movement that had begun at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seneca-falls-convention">Seneca Falls Convention</a> of 1848, although many women of colour remained excluded from voting in practice.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nineteenth-amendment-to-the-united-states-constitution.jpg" alt="Nineteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:19th_Amendment_Pg1of1_AC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
